  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-06T09:59:08.378Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the current beta build, it seems that images processed with focusing are too blurry than expectations.\nFor example, I took photos by the new built-in camera (the first one) and VirtualLens2 (the second one) with the following conditions:\n- Zoom is the default value of the built-in camera (focal length is about 23 [mm])\n- Aperture (F-Number) is about 4.0\n- Distance to the focus plane is about 3.0 [m]\n- Resolution is 3840x2160\nAccording to CoC equations, the diameter of bokeh should be less than 5 [px] under these conditions with a 35mm virtual image sensor, but it is greater than 30 [px] actually.\nTherefore, it seems there is something wrong with the DoF simulation. Could you fix this problem?\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_of_confusion#Determining_a_circle_of_confusion_diameter_from_the_object_field",
